# F5K — RC Electric Thermal Duration, Multiple-Task     seed definition, draft
# Rule refs: FAI Sporting Code Volume F5 Electric 2026 ed.2 (5.5.10.x)
# Provisional class.
#
# The class that pushes hardest on the model. Three of the six findings come
# from here: launch points measured relative to a parameter (F5), a per-launch
# cost that must read the flight's own sequence number (F6), and a task-total
# cap and a raw-score rounding with nowhere to live (F4).

class F5K
  name     "RC Electric Thermal Duration, Multiple-Task"
  fai      "F5K"
  version  "FAI F5 Electric 2026 ed.2"

  # The Nominal Launch Height: 60 m in light wind, 70 m in moderate wind,
  # announced by the CD one day before from the mean wind 11:00–17:00. The
  # textbook Parameter — a legitimate local choice, bound from measured
  # conditions before flying.
  param nlh            m    default 60 boundAt BeforeFlying   # 5.5.10.3
  param flyoffSize          no default                        # 5.5.10 — size not fixed by the rules (F12)
  param minPerGroup         no default                        # F5K states no group minimum (F12)
  param carryPenalties Flag no default                        # F5K states nothing (F12)
  param minRounds           no default                        # 5.5.10 states no minimum-rounds rule (F12)

  finalRanking LastPhaseReplaces                                     # 5.5.10.16 "fly-off replaces preliminary points"

  reflight
    entitled     Replacement                                         # 5.5.10.13
    others       BetterOf                                            # 5.5.10.13
    minNewGroup  4                                                   # 5.5.10.13

  penalty "motorRestartInFlight"    zeroFlight                       # 5.5.10.12 flight penalty c
  penalty "hitPersonOtherThanTimer" zeroRound                        # 5.5.10.12 safety penalty a
  penalty "safetyZone"              deduct 300                       # 5.5.10.12 safety penalty b, c "deducted from the final score"

  metricSet f5kFlight
    metric flightTime            Number s Truncate 1                 # 5.5.10.6 f whole seconds, tenths not rounded
    metric launchAltitude        Number m Truncate 1                 # 5.5.10.3 highest altitude to 10 s after motor stop
    metric landedInPilotArea     Flag                                # 5.5.10.15
    metric landedOnField         Flag                                # 5.5.10.12 flight penalty b — landing off the field = 0 for that flight
    metric overflewLandingWindow Flag                                # 5.5.10.12 flight penalty a

  # ========================================================================
  phase Preliminary

    rounds    ChooseFromCatalogue tasksPerRound 1                    # 5.5.10.2 one task per round from A–E
    validity  minRounds param(minRounds)                             # 5.5.10 defines no minimum-rounds rule, so the CD decides (F12)
    drop      ByRound 1 whenRounds >= 7                              # 5.5.10.16 "if 7 or more rounds are flown"

    # -- A ---------------------------------------------------------------
    # Four targets in any order; every flight counts whether or not its target
    # is reached, so the target is a clamp (as F3K K), not a Poker condition.
    task A "1, 2, 3, 4 minute flights in any order"                  # 5.5.10.2
      use       f5kFlight
      flights   bestN 4 targets anyOrder [60, 120, 180, 240] s       # 5.5.10.2
      timing    Fixed 600 s prep 300 s maxLaunches 4                 # 5.5.10.2; 5.5.10 preparation time >= 5 min per round
      group     minPerGroup param(minPerGroup)                       # F5K states no group minimum (F12)
      normalise HigherIsBetter winner 1000 round HalfUp 1            # 5.5.10.15 rounded to whole points
      rawScore  round Truncate 1                                     # 5.5.10.15 raw truncated down to whole points (F4b, adopted)
      # 5.5.10.12 flight penalty b zeroes THE FLIGHT, not the flight-time term
      # (F17). Written as a term wrapper it guarded only the first term, so a
      # model landing off the field still collected its launch-height
      # adjustment and its −10/−100 deductions. The gate belongs here, where it
      # zeroes every term at once and still leaves the flight selected —
      # "zero points for that flight only", so Task B's last flight stays last.
      # Inherited by B, C, D and E through `like`.
      flightValidWhen landedOnField == true                          # 5.5.10.12 flight penalty b
      score
        rate flightTime 1 pt/s cap 599 perTask                       # 5.5.10.15 1 pt/s; the assigned target caps each flight,
                                                                     # 5.5.10.2 "maximum total flight time used for scoring:
                                                                     #   9.59 min" caps the SUM (F4a, adopted). Not a cap on the
                                                                     #   raw score: the launch bonus below is added after it.
        # Launch points relative to the announced NLH. Cumulative bands read
        # from an origin: at NLH+15 the deduction is 10×1.0 + 5×3.0 = 25.
        # The below-NLH band has a NEGATIVE rate over a NEGATIVE portion,
        # which is what makes it a bonus.
        when flightTime >= 30                                        # 5.5.10.4 no bonus for flights shorter than 30 s
          then piecewise launchAltitude from param(nlh)              # origin (F5, adopted)
                 any..0   @ -0.5 pt/m                                # 5.5.10.4 each metre below NLH: +0.5 bonus
                 0..10    @ -1.0 pt/m                                # 5.5.10.4
                 10..any  @ -3.0 pt/m                                # 5.5.10.4
          else piecewise launchAltitude from param(nlh)              # penalties still apply under 30 s
                 0..10    @ -1.0 pt/m
                 10..any  @ -3.0 pt/m
        when landedInPilotArea == false
          then constant -10                                          # 5.5.10.15 −10 per landing outside the Pilot Area
        when overflewLandingWindow == true
          then constant -100                                         # 5.5.10.12 flight penalty a

    # -- B ---------------------------------------------------------------
    # Only the last flight counts — so the launch cost must be read off that
    # flight's own sequence number, which is the whole of finding F6.
    # B restates `score`, which replaces A's block entirely — so A's
    # `cap 599 perTask` does not reach B, and 5.5.10.2 states no 9:59 total for
    # it. Everything B does not restate, `rawScore` included, comes from A.
    task B "Last flight, 5 out of 7 minutes" like A                  # 5.5.10.2
      flights   last
      timing    Fixed 420 s prep 300 s maxLaunches 3
      score
        rate flightTime 1 pt/s cap 300 s                             # 5.5.10.2 maximum flight time 5 minutes
        when flightTime >= 30
          then piecewise launchAltitude from param(nlh)
                 any..0 @ -0.5 pt/m ; 0..10 @ -1.0 pt/m ; 10..any @ -3.0 pt/m   # 5.5.10.4
          else piecewise launchAltitude from param(nlh)
                 0..10 @ -1.0 pt/m ; 10..any @ -3.0 pt/m
        lookup flight.sequence                                       # intrinsic ref (F6, adopted)
          <= 1 ->   0 ;  <= 2 -> -10 ;  any -> -20                   # 5.5.10.2 Task B launch penalties (cumulative on the last flight)
        when landedInPilotArea == false then constant -10            # 5.5.10.15
        when overflewLandingWindow == true then constant -100        # 5.5.10.12 flight penalty a

    # -- C ---------------------------------------------------------------
    task C "All up, 4 minutes maximum (3x)" like A                   # 5.5.10.2
      flights   all
      timing    Fixed 241 s prep 15 s maxLaunches 3                  # 5.5.10.2 working time 4:01 PER launch (finding F13)
      score
        rate flightTime 1 pt/s cap 240 s                             # 5.5.10.2 maximum measured flight time 4 minutes
        when flightTime >= 30
          then piecewise launchAltitude from param(nlh)
                 any..0 @ -0.5 pt/m ; 0..10 @ -1.0 pt/m ; 10..any @ -3.0 pt/m   # 5.5.10.4
          else piecewise launchAltitude from param(nlh)
                 0..10 @ -1.0 pt/m ; 10..any @ -3.0 pt/m
        when landedInPilotArea == false then constant -10
        when overflewLandingWindow == true then constant -100

    # -- D ---------------------------------------------------------------
    task D "3, 3, 4 minute flights in any order" like A              # 5.5.10.2
      flights   bestN 3 targets anyOrder [180, 180, 240] s           # 5.5.10.2
      timing    Fixed 600 s prep 300 s maxLaunches 3
      # D restates no `score` and no `rawScore`, so both come whole from A —
      # including the `cap 599 perTask` on the flight-time term, which D needs
      # for the same reason A does: 180+180+240 = 600 s. 5.5.10.2.

    # -- E ---------------------------------------------------------------
    # Poker. Unlike F3K's, the launch cost applies to every launch made, so the
    # selection must be `all` — an unachieved flight scores no flight points
    # and no height adjustment, but still carries its launch penalty.
    task E "Poker" like A                                            # 5.5.10.2
      metric    targetTime Number s Truncate 1 declared              # 5.5.10.2 announced to, and recorded by, the timekeeper
      flights   all
      timing    Fixed 600 s prep 300 s maxLaunches 3
      score
        when flightTime >= targetTime                                # 5.5.10.2 marked "Y" — the pilot is credited with the target time
                                                                     # (landedOnField now gates the whole flight, not this term)
          then rate targetTime 1 pt/s cap 599                        # "any time over the target time is not counted";
                                                                     # 5.5.10.2 "the target and maximum allowable flight time
                                                                     #   is 9 minutes and 59 seconds" — per flight, not per task
        # 5.5.10.2: "the launch altitude bonus or penalty only applies where
        # the target time is achieved" — a second guard F5K's other tasks lack.
        when all(flightTime >= targetTime, flightTime >= 30)
          then piecewise launchAltitude from param(nlh)
                 any..0 @ -0.5 pt/m ; 0..10 @ -1.0 pt/m ; 10..any @ -3.0 pt/m   # 5.5.10.4
        lookup flight.sequence                                       # intrinsic ref (F6, adopted)
          <= 1 ->   0 ;  <= 2 -> -10 ;  any -> -20                   # 5.5.10.2 Task E: 2nd launch −10, 3rd a further −20
        when landedInPilotArea == false then constant -10
        when overflewLandingWindow == true then constant -100

  # ========================================================================
  # Whether this phase is flown at all is not class data. 5.5.10 makes the
  # fly-off mandatory for seniors at World and Continental Championships and
  # leaves it to the organiser everywhere else, so mandatoriness is conditional
  # on the event level — something the model has no notion of. A flag on the
  # phase could only ever have said "optional" here, and would have been wrong
  # at a championship.
  phase Flyoff                                                       # 5.5.10

    promotion TopN param(flyoffSize) group param(minPerGroup)..unlimited
                carryPenalties param(carryPenalties)                 # F5K states nothing about carry-over (F12)
                                                                     # 5.5.10 — F5K is SILENT on carry-over (finding F12)
    rounds    ChooseFromCatalogue tasksPerRound 1
    validity  minRounds 3                                            # 5.5.10 "if fewer than 3 complete, preliminary results stand"
    # no drop: 5.5.10 states no fly-off discard

    task A like Preliminary.A ; task B like Preliminary.B ; task C like Preliminary.C
    task D like Preliminary.D ; task E like Preliminary.E

# ---- unresolved for F5K --------------------------------------------------
# Tie-break (5.5.10.16: best dropped score, then a one-task tie-break fly-off)
# needs both kinds of tie-break and is not writable. Finding F15.
#
# Junior fly-off size = 2/3 of the senior fly-off size. Not writable: the model
# has no notion of competitor categories, and adding one would be a new domain
# concept. Stopped rather than added; flagged in findings (F18).
#
# Ruled (CD, 2026-08-01): a model landing off the flying field scores zero for
# that flight outright — the launch altitude is still recorded, but it cannot
# move a score that is already zero. This is why 5.5.10.12 flight penalty b sits
# on `flightValidWhen` and not on a score term. It changes one number as a side
# effect: in Task E a flight that lands off the field used to contribute its
# −10/−20 launch cost through the flight.sequence lookup and now contributes 0.
# That follows from "zero points for that flight" and is intended.
